'''Season twenty-four''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' premiered on March 20, 2017, on the [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] network.<ref name="premiere">{{cite web|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2017/01/17/abcs-number-one-hit-reality-show-dancing-with-the-stars-returns-with-an-all-new-season-on-monday-march-20-25012/20170117abc01/|title=Breaking News - ABC's Number One Hit Reality Show, "Dancing with the Stars," Returns with an All-New Season on Monday, March 20 - TheFutonCritic.com|work=thefutoncritic.com|access-date=1 March 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2016/tv/news/abc-renewals-the-goldbergs-1201721897/|title=ABC Renews 15 Shows Including 'Quantico,' 'The Bachelor' & Comedy Slate|first=Elizabeth|last=Wagmeister|date=3 March 2016|work=variety.com|access-date=1 March 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170210152342/http://variety.com/2016/tv/news/abc-renewals-the-goldbergs-1201721897/|archive-date=10 February 2017|url-status=live}}</ref>

On May 23, 2017, former [[NFL]] running back [[Rashad Jennings]] and [[Emma Slater]] were crowned the champions, while former [[MLB]] catcher [[David Ross (baseball)|David Ross]] and [[Lindsay Arnold]] finished in second place, and [[Fifth Harmony]] singer [[Normani]] and [[Val Chmerkovskiy]] finished in third.

==Cast==
===Couples===
This season featured twelve celebrity contestants. On February 21, 2017, [[Maksim Chmerkovskiy]] and [[Peta Murgatroyd]] were announced as the first two professionals returning this season.<ref>{{cite web |date=21 February 2017 |title='Dancing' stars Maksim Chmerkovskiy and Peta Murgatroyd to return to the show |url=https://abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/dancing-stars-maksim-chmerkovskiy-peta-murgatroyd-return-season/story?id=45622891 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170302083407/https://abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/dancing-stars-maksim-chmerkovskiy-peta-murgatroyd-return-season/story?id=45622891 |archive-date=2 March 2017 |access-date=1 March 2017 |work=ABC News}}</ref> In the following days, [[Lindsay Arnold]], [[Sharna Burgess]], [[Witney Carson]],  [[Artem Chigvintsev]], [[Valentin Chmerkovskiy]], [[Sasha Farber]], [[Gleb Savchenko]], and [[Emma Slater]] were all confirmed as professional dancers.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://people.com/tv/dancing-stars-fifth-harmony-normani-kordei-joins-season-24-sharna-burgess-jenna-johnson-return/?xid=socialflow_twitter_peoplemag|title=Fifth Harmony's Normani Kordei Joins Dancing with the Stars — Plus Find Out Which Pros Are Returning|date=24 February 2017|work=people.com|access-date=1 March 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170301180330/http://people.com/tv/dancing-stars-fifth-harmony-normani-kordei-joins-season-24-sharna-burgess-jenna-johnson-return/?xid=socialflow_twitter_peoplemag|archive-date=1 March 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> In addition, [[Kym Herjavec]] (who last competed in [[Dancing with the Stars (American season 20)|season 20]]) and [[Keo Motsepe]] (who last competed in [[Dancing with the Stars (American season 22)|season 22]]) were also confirmed as returning as professional dancers.

The full cast was announced on ''[[Good Morning America]]'' on March 1, 2017.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.etonline.com/tv/211588_kym_johnson_returning_for_dwts_season_24_celebrity_pairings_revealed/|title=EXCLUSIVE: Kym Johnson Returning for 'DWTS' Season 24, Celebrity Pairings Revealed|work=etonline.com|access-date=1 March 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170228164331/http://www.etonline.com/tv/211588_kym_johnson_returning_for_dwts_season_24_celebrity_pairings_revealed/|archive-date=28 February 2017|url-status=live}}</ref>

